# Build-time values for every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable an app's source references, one line per value:
#   <app> NAME=value
# Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the browser bundle when it BUILDS. The release builds with no
# Vercel credential (scripts/ci/vercel_offline_build.sh), so the project's environment is never
# pulled and these values must come from here. Only public-by-design values belong in this file:
# a reCAPTCHA site key is shipped to every visitor's browser. Never a secret, never a sensitive-type
# variable. Source of each value: the project's production environment in Vercel (read once with
# `vercel api`, no .env file written). The build refuses to run if an app's source references a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* name that is not listed here for that app, and checks the value ended up in the output.
# apps/admin references no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
booking NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=6LehHfMtAAAAAMnSpyX4xA_uN-mQm2pwHh03fNXs
